I've been playing nethack for a little under a month and I just reached
the boulders and pits levels last night. I got hungry while I was in
there and ended up eating a nymph corpse, oops. I had eaten a leprecaun
corpse in a previous game and swore off them for life. I'm doing so
well this game I don't want to jump somewhere bad so I was wondering if
I can get rid of the jumpy feeling. Does it time out or do I have to
hope that I can find a controlling item before I die stupidly?
I also had my first encounter with a trice type; of course I was blind
at the time so my first clue was feeling my limbs stiffen. I managed to
kill them, all three of them (praise Mars) and that was when I knew
that this would be a special game if only I can get rid of the
jumpiness.

BTW what a great game, I had played "Castle of the Winds" (basically a
comercial tiled Angband as far as I remember) when I was a kid and
later both "Baldurs Gate" games and Diabolo (my index finger hasn't
been the same since) and I had been looking for a game like BG but free
for a long time but non of the newer ones gave a really satisfing
experence. Then I discovered Nethack which is better than all of them
and easier on the fingers to boot!

Oh and I'm finally learning to *slow down*.

Cheers,
